{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>לא</b> — the meaning: one should not be astonished if the daughters commit harlotry, for it is their men who go up to the tops of the mountains to offer incense; they eat and drink with the harlots and harlot-worshippers, all of them." "<b>ומלת יפרדו</b> — men who are intimate with a single harlot." "<b>ומלת ילבט</b> — in the language of Ishmael, as if confounded, not knowing what to do; and like it: 'ואויל שפתים ילבט' (Proverbs 10:8). And behold, there is no meaning to <b>לא אפקוד</b> — that He will not punish them — but rather a matter against the fathers, for they teach them to commit harlotry, to do like their deeds. Perhaps the daughters are young; therefore, 'I will not punish.'"], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "Reading לעשות כמעשיהם as referring to the daughters being taught harlotry by the fathers; the syntax is compressed and the referent of 'them' is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:08.383991853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}